{"html":"<h1 id=\"get-started\">Get started</h1>\n<p><a href=\"./guide.html\">Guide</a> / How</p>\n<p>Select a release with browser support, then run and edit these examples without installing VKF. The browser security model is documented in the <a href=\"./browser.html\">embedding guide</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"run-and-change-a-program\">Run and change a program</h2>\n<p>Press <strong>Run</strong>, change <code>* 2</code> to <code>* 3</code>, then run again. The same function is applied through both the flat and nested vectors.</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-1\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.5</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-1\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Run and change a program\" spellcheck=\"false\">double(value:int) -&gt; int: value * 2\n\n:: double([1, 2, 3])\n:: double([[1, 2], [3, 4]])</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<p><code>value:int</code> declares the parameter type, <code>-&gt; int</code> the result type, and <code>:</code> the function body. <code>::</code> prints the result.</p>\n<p>Continue with <a href=\"./reference.html#1-programs-and-bindings\">bindings and values</a>, <a href=\"./reference.html#3-functions-and-calls\">functions</a>, or <a href=\"./reference.html#8-shapes-axes-and-indexing\">vectors and axes</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"make-it-visible\">Make it visible</h2>\n<p>Run this program, then edit a coordinate in <code>x</code> or <code>y</code> and run it again. The frame displays the structured data you supply.</p>\n<section class=\"readme-example\" data-vkf-example-id=\"example-2\"><div class=\"readme-example-bar\"><span>Run in browser · <span data-vkf-run-version>0.4.5</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"readme-example-play\">Run</button></div><div class=\"readme-example-layout\"><div class=\"readme-example-workspace\"><div class=\"readme-example-editor\"><pre class=\"readme-example-highlight\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><code></code></pre><textarea class=\"readme-example-source\" data-example-id=\"example-2\" aria-label=\"Editable VKF source: Make it visible\" spellcheck=\"false\">: .ui.display\n:.math\n\ndisplay: Display()\nframe: display.add_frame(pos:[0.08, 0.08], size:[0.84, 0.84])\n\nx: 0.1[..100] - 5\ny: sin(x)\n\nframe.add(\n    x_i:x,\n    y_i:y,\n    color:[0.12, 0.72, 1.0, 1.0]\n)</textarea></div><section class=\"readme-example-terminal\"><span>Console</span><pre class=\"readme-example-output\" aria-live=\"polite\"></pre></section></div></div></section>\n<p><a href=\"./concepts.html#graphics-and-interfaces\">The graphics model</a> → <a href=\"./ui-architecture.html\">rendering architecture</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"build-an-interface\">Build an interface</h2>\n<p>Use HTML and CSS for layout and styling, with VKF supplying calculations and behaviour. For a static webpage, the <a href=\"./browser.html\">browser embedding walkthrough</a> covers the bundle and host glue.</p>\n<p>The compiled HTML/CSS application runtime is currently a Windows native capability; it is not the same as embedding the browser subset. Inspect the <a href=\"./sources/examples/ui_plot_card/app.vkf\">VKF program</a>, <a href=\"./sources/examples/ui_plot_card/ui/main.html.txt\">HTML</a> and <a href=\"./sources/examples/ui_plot_card/ui/theme.css\">CSS</a> together.</p>\n<h2 id=\"run-locally-or-share-through-a-browser\">Run locally or share through a browser</h2>\n<p>For native work, <a href=\"./install.html#download-the-native-compiler\">download VKF</a>, run the <a href=\"./install.html#your-first-local-program\">first local program</a>, then use the <a href=\"./install.html#cli-walkthrough\">CLI</a>.</p>\n<p>For a website, <a href=\"./install.html#compile-the-browser-runtime-from-source\">build the browser runtime</a>, <a href=\"./browser.html\">embed it</a>, and follow the <a href=\"./install.html#host-it-without-an-application-backend\">static-hosting requirements</a>.</p>\n<p>The browser build recipe is not a general <code>vkf --wasm</code> export command. Its supported path and limitations are documented in the linked walkthrough.</p>\n<p><a href=\"./concepts.html\">What: core ideas and performance →</a> · <a href=\"./guide.html\">Back to guide</a></p>","headings":[{"level":1,"title":"Get started","id":"get-started"},{"level":2,"title":"Run and change a program","id":"run-and-change-a-program"},{"level":2,"title":"Make it visible","id":"make-it-visible"},{"level":2,"title":"Build an interface","id":"build-an-interface"},{"level":2,"title":"Run locally or share through a browser","id":"run-locally-or-share-through-a-browser"}],"examples":[{"id":"example-1","source":"double(value:int) -> int: value * 2\n\n:: double([1, 2, 3])\n:: double([[1, 2], [3, 4]])","title":"Run and change a program"},{"id":"example-2","source":": .ui.display\n:.math\n\ndisplay: Display()\nframe: display.add_frame(pos:[0.08, 0.08], size:[0.84, 0.84])\n\nx: 0.1[..100] - 5\ny: sin(x)\n\nframe.add(\n    x_i:x,\n    y_i:y,\n    color:[0.12, 0.72, 1.0, 1.0]\n)","title":"Make it visible"}],"source":"docs/site/getting-started.md","route":"getting-started.html","releaseCatalog":{"schema":"vektor-flow/release-catalog-v1","latest":"0.4.5","latestBrowserRuntime":{"version":"0.4.5","url":"https://vektorflow.org/runtimes/v0.4.5/vkf-shared-compiler.wasm?sha256=a1a1322a50df3db16c00550f484ea1145ac11f9e77a787a51653264203bccb06"},"releases":[{"version":"0.4.0","tag":"v0.4.0","status":"published","browserRuntimeWasm":null,"benchmarkTier":"feature","benchmark":{"summary":"Full 1,000-run 